<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Foral Community of Navarre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Foral Community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> is an autonomous community of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a>. It is the direct heir of the medieval Kingdom of Navarre: its special status rests on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ley-paccionada">Ley Paccionada</a> of 1841 and the Amejoramiento of 1982, and it collects its own taxes under an economic agreement with the Spanish state, a fiscal autonomy shared only with the Basque Country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/foral-community-of-navarre.jpg" alt="Foral Community of Navarre" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miguillen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandera_de_Navarra.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
